{
  "dom_id": "step-q104629",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Simplify the  expression\n${v}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{{v}^{5}}{{v}^{12}}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{v}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{{v}^{5}}{{v}^{12}} & = \\\\ {v}^{9}\\cdot {v}^{5-12} & = \\\\ {v}^{9}\\cdot {v}^{-7} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{v}^{9}\\cdot {v}^{-7} & = \\\\ {v}^{9+(-7)} & = \\\\ {v}^{9-7} & = \\\\ {v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{v}^{9}\\cdot \\frac{{v}^{5}}{{v}^{12}}={v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
